  FT["BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1"] = {"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":13,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"剧院、影院与娱乐附例 1954(1)","en":"THEATRE CINEMA AND ENTERTAINMENTS BY LAWS 1954(1)","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954(1).pdf》（6 页），本次切分 13 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954(1).pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7."},"text":{"en":"-(1) The area of the auditorium shall be not less than 3 Auditorium. square feet to each person to be admitted.\n\n(2) All floors and balconies shall be constructed in rein­ forced concrete or other approved materials.\n\n(3) The height between auditorium floor and ceiling shall be not less than 12 feet between balcony and ceiling not less than 10 feet.\n\n(4) There shall be provided:- A. A clear passage or gangway not less than 4 feet wide around the auditorium. B. Gangways not less than 4 feet wide running parallel to the seating in such position as the Board may decide.\n\n(5) No obstruction shall be allowed in any stairway or gang­ way and no standing or sitting by members of the public shall be permitted in any stairway or alley way.\n\n(6) Should steps occur in any gangway they shall be suitably illuminated during all preforrnances."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8."},"text":{"en":"-(1) Seats shall be ganged together in a row of not less Seating. than five, or each seat shall be securely fastened to the floor.\n\n(2) No seat is to be more than seven seats from a gangway, counted in the line of seating.\n\n(3) No barricades whatever shall be erected round indivi­ dual seats or blocks of seats.\n\n(4) When all seating space in the body of the hall or in the galleries is occupied, all booking shall cease and a notice shall be exhibited outside the entrance notifying that part or the whole of the theatre is full."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9."},"heading":{"en":"theatre except only the caretakers of the building and the proper-c<:ommo­"},"text":{"en":"No one shall be allowed to dwelL ledge or sleep in a Domestic ties, and these only to the number and in the rooms approved and ation. sanctioned by the Board."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10."},"heading":{"en":"-(1) All theatres shall be thoroughly cleaned and swept Cleaning"},"text":{"en":"-(1) All theatres shall be thoroughly cleaned and swept Cleaning by 9 a.m. each day and all offensive and waste matters removed. nd. . Latrines ana urinals shall he cleaned daily and no receptacle for anrtauon urine or nightsoil shall be placed in any part of the theatre except in the latrines and urinals approved by the Board.\n\n(2) There shall be provided:- A. One foot of urinal space for every 100 seats or' one urinal stall for every 200 seats. B. One male closet for every 200 seats. C. One female closet for every 100 seats,\n\n(3) The building is to be closed twice a year for such clea­ nsing, disinfecting, lime-washing; painting and repair work as may be considered necessary by the Board. Right of 11.-(1) Free access is to be given at all times for inspection Access. by the Board or their authorised agent.\n\n(2) No person shall enter the building between performances except on-business. Lighting. 12.-(1) No naked lights or fires are to be used in the building except with the specific approval of the Board in writing.\n\n(2) The building shall be fitted with secondary lighting of a type approved by the Board. Projection 13.-(1) Cinematograph projection apparatus is to be fixed Room. in an enclosure or room built of fire resisting material of suitable size to allow operators to work freely and the materials, construc­ tion and size must be to the approval of the Board.\n\n(2) This enclosure or room must be outside the auditorium if possible and fitted with a self closing fireproof door opening outwards, preferably onto an open space or landing fitted with railings where necessary.\n\n(3) This door must net be locked whilst the projection en­ closure is occupied.\n\n(4) All openings in front of the enclosure into the auditorium are to be glazed and these must not be more than two to each projection machine with a total area of not more than 1-!. square feet.\n\n(5) Each opening is to be fitted with a self closing metal shutter so arranged that they can be operated for closure by a release mechanism worked from the position of each projection machine and also from outside the door of the projection room.\n\n(6) Where possible there shall be no other opening, door or connection to the auditorium except the above mentioned projec­ tion openings.\n\n(7) Each projection machine shall have fitted above it a metal hood and vent opening into the open air outside the building. Rewind 14.---(1) The rewinding, pointing and piecing of films shall Room. not be carried out in the projection room but in a separate fire­ proof enclosure fitted with a door as for the projection room.\n\n(2) The table in this rewind room is to be surfaced with non­ ferrous metal (e.g. lead).\n\n(3) No smoke or fumes are to be allowed to escape from either room into the auditorium. Film 15.-(1) No film except such as are necessary for the imme­ diate. Storage. performance are to be stored in either the projection or rewind rooms.\n\n(2) Films may only be stcred in metal cases in a film storage vault, constructed of approved fire-proof material and situated out­ side and, where, possible, distinct from, the main or other building.\n\n(3) This vault it to be fitted with a self closing fire-proof door and must be adequately ventilated.\n\n(4) No naked lights are allowed in this vault.\n\n(5) No unauthorised shall be allowed in the pro­ person jection, rewind or film rooms or on the or in the storage stage dressing rooms."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16."},"heading":{"en":"There must be no smoking in tile projection, rewind,"},"text":{"en":"There must be no smoking in tile projection, rewind, Smoking. film or battery rooms or on tile and adequate notices storage stage, to this effect must be displayed ill prominent positions in and outside the rooms."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17."},"heading":{"en":"storage"},"text":{"en":"Any electrical battery or accumulator equipment Batteries. must be housed in a separate room."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18."},"heading":{"en":"are"},"text":{"en":"--(1) All electrical installations to be to the approval Electrical are Installaof both the Board and the local electricity company. tions.\n\n(2) No loose wires or connections are permitted."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19."},"heading":{"en":"-·(1) One properly trained fireman is to be provided or Fire"},"text":{"en":"-·(1) One properly trained fireman is to be provided or Fire obtained from the local fire for 300 with Precaution. brigade every seats a minimum of two and no performance is to start un-til such firemen have reported their to tile presence manager.\n\n(2) The following fire extinguishers must be provided, suit­ ably mounted and kept in good conditioru-> Four (or more be directed by tile Board) Soda­ as may acid type in auditorium. ,One Carbon tetra chloride (C.T.C.) type near electric switchboard on the stage. One C.T.C. quart size in office. Two 2-gallon foam type in projection' room. One 2-gallon feam ill film room. type storage One 2-gallon foam type in rewind room. One asbestos blanket correctly suspended for each pro­ jection machine."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20."},"heading":{"en":"system"},"text":{"en":"The ventilation must be of a type approved by Ventilation. the Board and of a capacity of not less than 1,000 cubic feet per hour. person per"}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21."},"heading":{"en":"may any Articles"},"text":{"en":"The following 110t be kept on the premises of theatre except by written permission of the Board and then only not allowed. in such direct:- quantities as they may\n\n(a) Petroleum.\n\n(b) Explosive.\n\n(c) Beer, Spirits and Wines."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22."},"heading":{"en":"person any Licence for"},"text":{"en":"(1) No shall utilize theatre witheut first obtaining a licence from the Board. This licence shall be in the Perforrnanform shown in Appendix A hereto. ces.\n\n(2) No performances will be allowed which will interfere with traffic, or be likely to cause a nuisance, obstruction or danger to tile public or to individuals resident in the locality."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23."},"heading":{"en":"who will in permission for hours between 9 a.m. Performan-"},"text":{"en":"The hours of performances shall be decided by the Board Hours of general give to 1.00 ces. a.m."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-1954-THEATRE-CINEMA-AND-ENTERTAINMENTS-BY-LAWS-1954-1-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24."},"heading":{"en":"Censorship"},"text":{"en":"-(1) All films before being shown in the theatre shall be inspected by the Board at such time shall be appointed, and of films. as no film shall be exhibited until passed by the Board.\n\n(2) Any film which has been passed by the the Official Censor of Cinematograph Film for Singapore and the Federation of Malaya may, unless the Board otherwise directs, be exhibited without having been so inspected. Permit for 25. No building shall be used as a theatre without a permit Theatre. to this effect being' issued by the Board. This permit shall be prominently displayed within the main entrance to the building, and shall state the time during which it is valid, and shall be in the form shown in Appendix \"B\" hereto. Fees. 26.-(1) Fees payable for a permit to use a building as a theatre shall be as follows:- Number of seats. Fee per day. Fee per mensem. Not more than 200 $ 1.-$10.- Not more than 500 $ 2.-$20.- Not more than 1000 s 5.--$25.-- Above 1000 $10.--$50.--\n\n(2) The permit fees may be reduced or waived by the Board where the use as a theatre is for a limited time or where the show is for charitable purposes or where no admission charges are made.\n\n(3) Fees payable for the issue of a licence for performance shall be as follows:-- Cinematograph $3.-$100.- Combined cinematograph and theatre performance $3.-s 75.- All other performances $3.-$ 50.-\n\n(4) The licence fees may be reduced or waived at the dis­ cretion of the Board, for shows where no fee is charged for admis­ sion or shows for charitable purposes. Penalty. 27.-(1) The holder of a licence or permit who allows any contravention of these By-laws by any member of his staff or other person, shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $500.\n\n(2) Any other person contravening any of these By-laws shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $100. I. O. GILBERT, British Resident, Brunei. APPENDIX \"A\". THE SANITARY BOARDS ENACTMENT, CAP. 57. THEATRE, CINEMA AND ENTERTAINMENT By-LAWS, 1954. ENTERTAINMENT LICENCE. Name of Licensee Address of Licensee Location of Theatre Type of Theatre Permit number of Theatre Name of holder of Permit Duration of Permit: From To Type of Show Date of Commencement Date of Termination Hours of Performance: From To .. Fee $ Note-This licence is granted subject to full compliance with the By-laws of the Board and also with the under­ mentioned special conditions or waivers:- Issued by on the Authority of the Board. APPENDIX \"B\". THE SANITARY BOARDS ENACTMENT, CAP. 57. THEATRE, CINEMA AND ENTERTAINMENT By-LAWS, 1954. THEATRE PERMIT. Name of holder of permit . Location of Theatre . Size of Theatre . Address of holder of permit . Type of Entertainment . Date of Commencement of permit . Date of Termination of permit . Fee $ . Licence granted on the undernoted conditions:- Municipal Officer."}}],"pack":"bn-p29","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"THEATRE CINEMA AND ENTERTAINMENTS BY LAWS 1954(1)","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-C6F030"] = {"id":"BN-S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-C6F030","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"SECTION","title":{"zh":"文莱达鲁萨兰国宪法修正命令 2024","en":"CONSTITUTION OF BRUNEI DARUSALAM AMENDMENT ORDER 2024","orig":null},"level":"regulation","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2024.pdf》（4 页），本次切分 5 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-ORDER-2024.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-C6F030-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"heading":{"en":"Citation and commencement"},"text":{"en":"This Order may be cited as the Constitution of Brunei Darussalam (Amendment) Order, 2024 and shall commence on the day it is made."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-C6F030-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of Article 2 of Const. I"},"text":{"en":"Article 2 of the Constitution of Brunei Darussalam, in this Order referred to as the Constitution, is amended, in Clause (1) - fa} by deleting the definition of \"Deputy Sultan\" and by substituting the following new definition therefor - \" \"Deputy Sultan\" means - fa} the person appointed by His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan under section 17 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959; or fb} during the Interim Period, the persons performing for and on behalf of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan under section 12 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959;\"; fb} by deleting the definition of \" \"His Majesty\" or \"His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan\" \" and by substituting the following new definition therefor\" \"His Majesty\" or \"His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan\" means a Sultan whose accession to the throne has been proclaimed whether or not he has been crowned as His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan of Brunei Darussalam, irrespective of whether a declaration has been made and confirmed under section 12 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959 that he is, by reason of his incapacity to make decisions, incapable for the time being of performing the State functions;\"; {c) by inserting the following new definition immediately after the definition of \"instrument\" - \" \"Interim Period\" means the period between the time of the confirmation under subsection (1) of section 12 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959 by the Council of Succession and the lawful Successor declared under subsection (2) of section 3 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959 that His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan is incapable for the time being of performing the State functions and the time of the declaration under subsection ( 1) or (2A) of section 12 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959, whichever is the earlier, that His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan has the capacity to make decisions;\"."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-C6F030-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of Article 6"},"text":{"en":"Article 6 of the Constitution is amended, in Clause (1A), by deleting \"the lawful Successor declared under subsection (2) of section 3 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959, the Deputy Sultan and the Regent,\" from the first three lines."}},{"id":"BN-S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-C6F030-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4."},"heading":{"en":"Amendment of Article 7"},"text":{"en":"Article 7 of the Constitution is amended - fa} by deleting Clause (1) and by substituting the following new Clause therefor\" ( 1) The Privy Council shall not be summoned except - fa) by the authority of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan; or {b) during the Interim Period, by the Deputy Sultan.\"; {b) by inserting the following new Clause immediately after Clause (1) - \"(1A) For the avoidance of doubt, the Privy Council shall not be summoned by the Deputy Sultan appointed under section 17 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959.\". Amendment of Article 8"}},{"id":"BN-S-42-2024-CONSTITUTION-OF-BRUNEI-DARUSALAM-AMENDMENT-C6F030-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5."},"heading":{"en":"CONSTITUTION OF BRUNEI DARUSSALAM"},"text":{"en":"Article 8 of the Constitution is amended - fa} in Clause (1), by deleting\", so far as practicable,\";\n\n(b) by deleting Clause (2) and by substituting the following new Clause therefor\"(2) In the event that His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan is declared and confirmed to be, by reason of his incapacity to make decisions, incapable for the time being of performing the State functions under subsection (1) of section 12 of the Succession and Regency Proclamation, 1959, the person who shall preside shall be the Deputy Sultan defined as such during the Interim Period.\". Made this 17th. day of Rabiulakhir, 1446 Hijriah corresponding to the 21st. day of October, 2024 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN, BRUNEI DARUSSALAM."}}],"pack":"bn-p29","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"CONSTITUTION OF BRUNEI DARUSALAM AMENDMENT ORDER 2024","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
  FT["BN-S-43-1998-EMERGENCY-MINOR-OFFENCES-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1998"] = {"id":"BN-S-43-1998-EMERGENCY-MINOR-OFFENCES-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1998","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam (AGC) — LAWS OF BRUNEI / Government Gazette","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-11","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":"紧急轻微罪行法修正命令 1998","en":"MERGENCY MINOR OFFENCES ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 1998","orig":null},"level":"law","status":"active","issuingBody":"Attorney General's Chambers, Brunei Darussalam","completenessNote":"来源为 AGC 官方 PDF《S-43-1998-EMERGENCY-MINOR-OFFENCES-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1998.pdf》（1 页），本次切分 1 条。该 PDF 为扫描件 + OCR 文本层，正文按版式位置重建：已剔除页眉页脚与边栏条标题、回接折行；未改写措辞、未增删内容。OCR 层面可能存在个别粘连或形近字，逐字引用请以原始 PDF 为准。","textQuality":"ocr-scanned","sourceFile":"S-43-1998-EMERGENCY-MINOR-OFFENCES-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1998.pdf","country":"BN","countryName":"文莱","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"BN-S-43-1998-EMERGENCY-MINOR-OFFENCES-ACT-AMENDMENT-ORDER-1998-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1."},"text":{"en":"BRUNEI DARUSSALAM GOVERNMENT GAZETTE No. S 43\n\nCONSTITUTION OF BRUNEI DARUSSALAM (Order under section 83(3l) EMERGENCY (MINOR OFFENCES ACT) (AMENDMENT) ORDER, 1998 In exercise of the power conferred by subsection (3) of section 83 of the Constitution of Brunei Darussalam, His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan hereby makes the following OrderCitation. 1. This Order may be cited as the Emergency (Minor Offences Act) (Amendment) Order, 1998. Addition of 2. The Minor Offences Act is amended by adding the following new Part to Chapter 30. HPARTIX\n\nCOMPOUNDING OF OFFENCES \"Compounding 38A. ( 1) The Chairman of any Municipal Board, any of offences. police officer not below the rank of Superintendent, and any person authorised by name or by office by the Minister by notification in the Gazette, may in his discretion, in relation to an offence under section 12 or to any offence under this Act which has been prescribed under subsection (3) as an offence which may be compounded, if he is satisfied that any other person has committed such offence and whether or not a prosecution is actually pending, compound such offence by collecting from that other person a sum of money not exceeding $500.\n\n(2) Any sum of money collected under this section shall be dealt with as if it were a fine imposed by a Court of a Magistrate.\n\n(3) The Minister with the approval of His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan may make rules to prescribe the offences which may be compounded under subsection ( 1) and the method and procedure thereof.\". Made this 4th. day of Syaaban 1419 Hijriah corresponding to the 23rd. day of November, 1998 at Our Istana Nurul Iman, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.\n\nHIS MAJESTY\n\nTHE SULTAN AND YANG DI-PERTUAN\n\nBRUNEI DARUSSALAM Dicetak oleh A WANG MOHIDIN BIN HAJI DAUD, Pemangku Pengarah Percetakan, di Jabatan Percetakan Kerajaan, Bandar Seri Begawan BB 3510, Negara Brunei Darussalam. Harga B$5.00"}}],"pack":"bn-p29","titleTranslation":{"engine":"llm","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewed":false,"batch":"CALR-TITLE-20261017-1801-BN-1261","source":"MERGENCY MINOR OFFENCES ACT AMENDMENT ORDER 1998","note":"由翻译 agent 按《法规标题中译规范》产出，经 tools/verify-title-return.js 机器校验后入库；尚未人工复核。"}};
